So `...` is a `Spread` node containing `VariableName`. So for `f(...args)`: ArgList children = `(`, Spread(contains VariableName), `)`. Counting non-paren/comma = 1 (the Spread node). But my earlier count returned 2. Why? Because in my walk, when I descend into ArgList and then into Spread's children... wait, I count only direct children of ArgList. The count loop `do { exprs++ unless paren/comma } while(nextSibling())` — children of ArgList are `(`, Spread, `)`. So exprs should be 1 (Spread). But it returned 2. Hmm. 

